.TH DISPLAYMANAGER 1 "November 2026" "0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
displaymanager \- control inputs, Picture-by-Picture and KVM on Dell monitors
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B displaymanager
.br
.B displaymanager
[\fB\-q\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Without arguments, opens the graphical application. With a command, performs
the action over DDC/CI using \fBddcutil\fR(1) and exits; this is what the
optional GNOME keyboard shortcuts call.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show monitor, inputs, PBP and KVM state.
.TP
.B switch
In Picture-by-Picture mode move keyboard and mouse to the other computer;
otherwise switch the full-screen input between this and the other computer.
.TP
.BR "usb " [ here | away | toggle ]
Move the monitor's USB hub (KVM).
.TP
.BR "layout " [ list | next | \fINAME\fR]
List or select the screen layout:
.BR single ,
.BR 50-50 ,
.BR 75-25 ,
.BR 80-20 ,
.BR 25-75 ,
.BR 20-80 ,
.BR pip-small ,
.BR pip-large .
.B next
cycles through the multi-input layouts.
.TP
.BR "pbp on" | off | toggle
Switch between the last used multi-input layout and a single input.
.TP
.B swap
Swap the left and right Picture-by-Picture sides.
.TP
.BI "input " CODE
Select the (left) input by hex VCP code, e.g. 0x0f.
.TP
.BI "right " CODE
Select the Picture-by-Picture right-side input.
.TP
.B inputs
List the inputs reported by the monitor.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Do not show a desktop notification.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/displaymanager/config.json
Settings, input names and overridable vendor VCP codes.
.SH NOTES
The user needs read/write access to the monitor's /dev/i2c-* device. The
ddcutil package grants this to the user logged in at the local desktop;
otherwise add the user to the \fBi2c\fR group.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ddcutil (1)
